.TH AQTRUNCAT 1 "2026-10-27" "AQTRunCat 2.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aqtruncat \- A Cute Run Cat for Linux: CPU\-driven tray runner with system metrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aqtruncat
.RI [ run " options]"
.br
.B aqtruncat run
.RB [ \-\-runner
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-fps
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.br
.B aqtruncat settings
.br
.B aqtruncat runner list
.br
.B aqtruncat runner import
.I FILE.zip
.RB [ \-\-id
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B aqtruncat runner remove
.I ID
.br
.B aqtruncat metrics
.RB [ \-\-watch ]
.br
.B aqtruncat autostart
.BR enable | disable | status
.br
.B aqtruncat
.BR \-h | \-\-help | \-v | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aqtruncat
shows an animated runner in the system tray (StatusNotifierItem) whose speed
follows the CPU load: 10 frames per second when idle, up to 40 at full load,
or the reverse with "Slow down under load". Left\-click the runner to show or
hide the Dashboard with CPU, memory, swap, network, storage and disk activity;
the context menu opens Settings and quits.
.PP
Run
.B aqtruncat settings
to open the same Settings window in its own process, without starting the tray.
It can also be opened from the AQTRunCat Settings application-menu entry, the
tray menu, the Plasma widget popup, or with
.BR "aqtruncatctl settings open" .
Closing Settings exits only that window process. The backend is activated on
demand and remains running after Settings closes; the Qt Tray Plugin and the
Plasma widget have independent lifecycles.
.PP
Custom Metrics may be RunCat Neo compatible JSON snapshots written by other
programs, or command configurations that periodically run an explicit
executable plus argument list and consume one UTF\-8 scalar output line.
Commands never use an implicit shell. The optional Metrics Bar shows up to
three compact values as extra tray icons next to the runner.
.PP
Built\-in metrics cover CPU, memory, swap, network, storage and disk I/O, and
also uptime, every GPU (utilization, memory, temperature where the driver
reports them), game FPS read from the log MangoHud writes, available package
and Flatpak updates (read\-only checks of the locally cached metadata unless a
remote refresh is enabled; nothing is ever installed), the kernel and the
distribution.
.PP
The metrics, Custom Metrics, integrations, runner speed and settings are
provided by the backend
.BR aqtruncatd ,
which the tray application starts on demand and which keeps running until the
session ends; the tray is one of its clients.
.B aqtruncatctl
reads and controls the same backend (see
.BR "aqtruncatctl \-\-help" ).
The D\-Bus API is
.B io.github.psykedady.AQTRunCat1
on the session bus.
.PP
On KDE Plasma 6 the same backend also feeds the
.B AQTRunCat
widget (Plasmoid
.BR io.github.psykedady.aqtruncat ),
added from Add or Manage Widgets. The widget and the tray application are
independent frontends: either, both or neither can run.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Start the tray application (the default without a command).
.B \-\-runner
selects a runner,
.B \-\-fps
sets a fixed diagnostic frame rate (1\-120, CPU load ignored),
.B \-\-verbose
logs CPU samples and frame rate decisions.
.TP
.B runner list
List bundled and user runners, including invalid ones and why.
.TP
.B runner import \fIFILE.zip\fR
Install a runner from a ZIP archive such as a Runner Gallery
.IR name \-frames.zip ;
nothing is installed if any check fails.
.B \-\-id
installs under another id,
.B \-\-force
replaces a user runner with the same id.
.TP
.B runner remove \fIID\fR
Uninstall a user runner. Bundled runners cannot be removed.
.TP
.B metrics
Print the system metrics once, or once per second with
.BR \-\-watch .
Update counts come from the backend:
.BR "aqtruncatctl metrics" .
.TP
.B autostart enable\fR|\fBdisable\fR|\fBstatus
Start AQTRunCat at login: the same per\-user preference as the Settings
window, applied as an XDG autostart entry.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/AQTRunCat/AQTRunCat.ini
Settings (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/AQTRunCat/runners/
User runners (default
.IR ~/.local/share ).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/AQTRunCat/metrics/
Custom Metrics standalone JSON files and immediate package/metric.json files
discovered automatically.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/aqtruncat.desktop
Autostart entry.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 failure, 2 invalid command line, 3 not found, 4 invalid runner
or archive, 5 conflict (already installed, bundled runner protected).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_LOGGING_RULES
Qt logging categories, e.g.
.BR aqtruncat.*.debug=true .
Without a terminal, Qt logs go to the journal.
.SH SEE ALSO
The README and documentation in
.IR /usr/share/doc/aqtruncat/ .
The optional Claude Code and Codex integrations (usage limits as in Claude
Code's /usage and Codex's /status) are enabled in Settings, Integrations,
or with
.B aqtruncat-claude-metric enable
and
.B aqtruncat-codex-metric enable
(see their
.BR --help ) .
